---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: casuals.html
nav: casuals
title: Casuals — SwiftPune
description: "SwiftPune casuals: once a month, a weekend brunch in Pune with no talks and no agenda. Meet the community, talk about what you're building, split the bill. Students welcome."
ogImage: assets/Events/Casuals/003/01.jpg
habits:
  - key: "// when"
    title: Once a month, over brunch.
    text: A weekend brunch at a restaurant somewhere in Pune. The place and time go up in the WhatsApp group first.
  - key: "// agenda"
    title: Meet people. That's it.
    text: No talks and no slides. Tell people what you're building, hear what they are, and get to know the community.
  - key: "// the bill"
    title: We split it.
    text: There's no ticket. Everyone pays their share of the bill at the table.
  - key: "// who"
    title: Students welcome.
    text: Working developers, designers, students, the curious. You don't need to have come to a meetup first.
---
{#- Casuals and watch parties live in src/_data/casuals.js — add them there. -#}
{%- import "macros/events.njk" as ev with context %}
{%- set latest = casuals.events[0] %}
{%- set annual = casuals.annual %}
{{ ev.hero(
  "// program.casuals",
  'No talks. Just <span class="ink">brunch</span>.',
  "Once a month we take a long table at a restaurant in Pune and
            spend a weekend brunch together. No agenda beyond meeting each
            other: talk about what you're building, hear what everyone else
            is up to, and put faces to the names in the group chat.",
  latest.photos.items[0],
  null,
  [
    { href: site.whatsapp, label: "Join the next one on WhatsApp", primary: true },
    { href: "#wwdc", label: "The WWDC watch party", arrow: false }
  ]
) }}

      <!-- ===========================================================
           How a casual works
           =========================================================== -->
      <section class="section section--program reveal" id="how">
        <div class="container">
          <ul class="habits" aria-label="How a casual works">
            {%- for h in habits %}
            <li class="habits__item">
              <p class="habits__key">{{ h.key }}</p>
              <h2 class="habits__title">{{ h.title }}</h2>
              <p class="habits__text">{{ h.text }}</p>
            </li>
            {%- endfor %}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ===========================================================
           Casuals — latest casual, then every casual.
           =========================================================== -->
      <section class="section section--program section--casuals reveal" id="casuals">
        <div class="container">
{{ ev.feature(latest, casuals.latestLabel) }}

{{ ev.log(casuals.events, casuals.logLabel) }}
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ===========================================================
           Annual special — the WWDC watch party.
           =========================================================== -->
      <section class="section section--program section--casuals section--annual reveal" id="wwdc">
        <div class="container">
          <header class="section-head annual-head">
            <p class="comment-eyebrow">// once_a_year</p>
            <h2 class="display">
              One night a year, we just <span class="ink">watch</span>.
            </h2>
            <p class="lead">
              The one casual with a screen in it. Every June the community
              gets in one room for the WWDC keynote and reacts to it
              together, which is still the best way to watch it.
            </p>
          </header>

{{ ev.feature(annual.events[0], annual.latestLabel, true, "h3") }}
{%- if annual.events.length > 1 %}

{{ ev.log(annual.events, annual.logLabel) }}
{%- endif %}
        </div>
      </section>
